images.prompt:
Create a completely NEW replacement illustration for a Chinese technical project's Markdown documentation. Use case: scientific-educational infographic. Asset 1 of a cohesive set for CallBridge. Landscape 3:2, high resolution. The old infographic was rejected for too much text and too many boxes. Do NOT make a document full of cards. Make an elegant, inviting editorial illustration with charming original animated-film-style characters, soft shapes, sophisticated flat 2.5D, thin dark outlines, warm off-white background, muted sage green, sky blue and apricot accents. Generous negative space, warm and professional, no clutter. Strong clear large Chinese typography. Main title, exact: "声音的一次旅行". Tiny eyebrow: "01 / AUDIO LIFECYCLE".
Show a continuous simple left-to-right path across the central scene, six visually distinct stations with large illustrations and arrows connecting IN THIS ORDER:
1 a friendly young adult speaking, label "你说话";
2 a physical microphone and a tiny ADC chip with analog wave turning into dots, label "麦克风 · ADC";
3 a Mac-shaped computer with sound samples, label "Core Audio";
4 a tiny app window encoding samples into packets next to a network cloud, label "通话软件 · 网络";
5 a receiver computer and DAC chip converting dots back into waveform, label "对端 · DAC";
6 another friendly young adult wearing headphones, smiling, label "对方听见".
Illustrations are the focus, not text. Use only the above main labels, plus a single discreet bottom transformation ribbon, exact "声波 → 电信号 → 数字样本 → 网络数据 → 声音". Large enough labels to read without zoom. About 65% illustration, 25% empty space, 10% text. Avoid explanation paragraphs, tiny footnotes, repeated headings, nested boxes, 15-step diagram, code snippets, implementation statuses, decorative meaningless connectors. Technical accuracy: ADC before digital Core Audio, DAC after network reception, no microphone capture in the receiving headphone station. Friendly original people, not copyrighted mascots. This is the CLASSICAL audio lifecycle, not the CallBridge text-to-speech pathway. Deliver a polished finished diagram as an image, not a mockup on a wall.
